Local instrumentation (not upstream): expose the swallowed P2P mailbox status.

kbusSetupMailboxes_GM200 configures the PCIe write-mailbox by RPC to GSP
(NV2080_CTRL_CMD_INTERNAL_BUS_SETUP_P2P_MAILBOX_LOCAL / _REMOTE), then checks
the result with NV_ASSERT(). NV_ASSERT compiles out in a release build, so if
GSP refuses these calls for CMP device IDs the driver carries on as though the
mailbox were live -- which matches the observed failure exactly: peer access
enables, cudaMemcpyPeer returns no error, and zero bytes are delivered.

This prints both RPC statuses plus the addresses involved, and reads back
NV_P2P_WREQMB_L/H for the peer being configured. Decision tree:

  RPC != NV_OK                    -> GSP is refusing; must program directly
  RPC == NV_OK but WREQMB stays 0 -> GSP silently no-ops the request
  WREQMB programmed, copies fail  -> routing/HSHUB, not the mailbox

Also logs the connection type actually selected, to confirm we are on the
PCIE_PROPRIETARY (mailbox) path rather than BAR1.

--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/arch/maxwell/kern_bus_gm200.c	2026-08-06 22:17:11.847445146 -0700
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/arch/maxwell/kern_bus_gm200.c	2026-08-06 22:17:34.822107930 -0700
@@ -127,6 +127,13 @@
